  "2026-10-22T19:20:59.097Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up review after orchestrator extension: rechecked clean worktree and released in-progress item, pulled remote 40a63c87 and merged origin/main because the branch was behind by one dependency/template commit. npm ci passed with zero audit vulnerabilities; pins were not independently changed. Previously fixed findings remain complete. New unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6vLTfT is valid: non-git recoveryCommands contains a shell placeholder and alternative workflows rather than executable tag-history repairs. Return an empty list, retain alternatives in the message, clarify usage/release recovery docs. New real plain-tracker regression covers all three tag flags with git available and absent. Initial test failed 1/1 on the actual command list versus expected empty list; isolated behavioral revert and full unchanged npm/Bun gates follow. Latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-22T19:25:50.684Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6vLTfT fixed: assertReleaseTagHistory now supplies [] outside Git or when git cannot execute; alternative tracker workflows remain only in prose. Self-review checked every MissingTagHistoryError construction, its consumers and milestone diagnostics: shallow/no-tags cases retain executable fetch/config recovery; the remaining milestone-name placeholder belongs to a human-readable remedy, not this executable command list. Clarified usage and release docs. Behavioral revert: restoring only the prior assertReleaseTagHistory implementation makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"non-git tag refusals\" test/milestones.test.ts fail 1/1 (exit 1), actual two milestone workflow commands versus expected empty array. Restored source rebuilt; focused milestone suite 11/11, adjacent shallow/full/no-tags controls plus new regression 4/4, pm-linked new regression 1/1; all zero failures/skips. npm ci/build/build:test/docstring (18 files/180 declarations) and whitespace checks passed. Full npm/Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds follow after push; no old fix or history record was rewritten."
  "2026-10-22T19:34:05.600Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up source head 18bc228aa793ece00525c19cbefe73c6e6cf8ad4 passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39840186537: npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22 and 26 each passed 794/794 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos (3176 passing executions). All gates retained 100% lines/branches/functions across 15 measured source files and 18 files/180 documented declarations; direct Bun CLI/SDK smoke passed 2/2 in each job. Tracker health, audit, pack, changelog/link/date and attestation checks passed. The new failing behavioral revert and restored 11/11 milestone, 4/4 adjacent and 1/1 pm-linked checks are recorded above. Local clean-HOME npm attempt was unfinished with no failure reported before being stopped after clean CI passed; it is not a passing local gate. Rechecked threads: only the addressed thread remains unresolved; latest CodeRabbit body still has no outside-diff finding. No new PM CLI/SDK bug established. Existing statement metric and custom-folder limits remain separately tracked. Release claim without closing the in-progress item; final tracker-only receipt commit will receive its own CI run."
  "2026-10-22T20:27:18.044Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator follow-up: pulled remote head and merged origin/main before edits. Blocking late-close attribution confirmed: only the first closed capture may own a release entry; open captures must not reserve release membership. Also verify monotonic offset-bearing capture times, compact render-input snapshots, non-git diagnostics/contract notice, CLI source conflicts, Git-resolved projection counts, portable milestone names, and existing direct Bun runtime coverage. Preserve completed fixes; add independent failing revert proofs and unchanged full npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-22T20:50:12.890Z",codex-agent,"Blocking attribution now uses each ID's first closed capture and its own frozen row. Open captures never reserve ownership; live closures remain Unreleased until captured closed. Strict RFC3339 offsets/calendar validation, strictly advancing instants, tied-order refusal and locked final publication guard prevent clock reordering. Snapshot creation and certified SDK reads retain only rendering/classification/ordering inputs, omit bodies/descriptions/comments/unrelated metadata and linked notes, and reject body-preview in milestone CLI/host flows. New names are lowercase portable tokens with reserved-device and legacy case-variant checks. Ignored pm-bin/pm-arg options now refuse. Dubious Git ownership has a separate diagnostic and exact-directory recovery after trust verification; corrected stale comment. A generated compatibility notice documents the non-git tag contract through the project changelog entrypoint; the new script is added to measured coverage with thresholds unchanged. Git-resolved projection counts were already correct; real tagged-tracker reopened-row regressions now cover all CLI/host summary and semver/explain paths. Bun script gate is explicitly labeled as such and existing direct Bun CLI/SDK smoke remains independently guarded. Self-review covered each attribution/input-projection/source-option/count consumer and storage name/clock paths."
  "2026-10-22T20:50:18.682Z",codex-agent,"Twelve independent behavioral revert proofs (each one assertion failure, exit 1, followed by restoration; CLI/extension dist rebuilt around applicable reverts): closed-attribution: node --test --test-name-pattern open milestone members test/milestones.test.ts; monotonic-publication: node --test --test-name-pattern directory publication serializes test/milestones.test.ts; offset-validation: node --test --test-name-pattern RFC3339 offsets test/milestones.test.ts; snapshot-projection: node --test --test-name-pattern milestone snapshots omit bodies test/milestones.test.ts; portable-names: node --test --test-name-pattern case variants test/milestones.test.ts; git-ownership: node --test --test-name-pattern dubious Git ownership test/milestones.test.ts; cli-source-conflicts: node --test --test-name-pattern real plain tracker CLI test/milestones.test.ts; extension-body-conflict: node --test --test-name-pattern real plain tracker CLI test/milestones.test.ts; git-cli-counts: node --test --test-name-pattern Git-resolved non-change counts test/release-membership.test.ts; git-extension-counts: node --test --test-name-pattern Git-resolved non-change counts test/release-membership.test.ts; compatibility-notice: node --test --test-name-pattern generated changelog declares test/milestones.test.ts; bun-runtime-guard: node --test --test-name-pattern CI retains test/release-workflow.test.ts. Fixed focused milestone/history/workflow suites passed 52/52 before the final presence/diagnostic assertions. Six core regressions were also red on the initial code. Latest complete review read has no unresolved threads or outside-diff findings; the supplied orchestrator findings govern this round."
  "2026-10-22T20:50:23.642Z",codex-agent,"Required main merge produced a pending tracker receipt. Pinned reconciliation first refused absent staged evidence; its guarded stage option then failed on the ignored sidecar directory. Reviewed the generated public hash-only sidecar, explicitly staged that single path, and reconciled successfully with zero drift. No manual history repair or re-anchor command was run. Preserve this SDK staging UX gap in the final report."
  "2026-10-22T21:02:07.917Z",codex-agent,"Corrected the added empty pm-bin test to expect the existing parser value error; this was an assertion mismatch, not a product failure. The affected pm-linked commands pass on retry: milestone suite 21/21 and milestone/workflow suite 39/39, each zero failures; the other two linked commands passed 1/1 each. Self-review then reproduced a same-name writer interleaving using real SQL storage: another writer commits between read and names, and the creation guard incorrectly rejected the idempotent retry. Skip the same candidate name during preliminary chronology checks; final locked publication and original membership verification still govern the result. New concurrent/compact controls pass 2/2. Thirteenth independent revert restored only assertCaptureOrder from source 70f3887: node --test --test-name-pattern \"concurrent same-name\" test/milestones.test.ts fails 1/1, exit 1, unexpected clock refusal. Restored source and rebuilt dist; build/build:test/docstrings pass. Live main advanced during work with PR 267, causing GitHub to withhold pull-request CI; commit this verified increment, merge current origin/main, preserve both feature paths and rerun complete gates."
  "2026-10-22T21:05:50.133Z",codex-agent,"Merged current origin/main 0bea2b5 (PR 267) after it advanced during the round. Resolved CLI/extension/API/manifest/workflow/docs conflicts by preserving both features, audit alias/report behavior, resolved-row counts, milestone source selection and direct native Bun smoke; regenerated dist and passed build/build:test/docstrings (20 files/184 declarations). New real plain-tracker integration passes 1/1: standalone audit --milestones and host changelog audit with milestones inspect the frozen closed row after live reopening, retain test_result gaps and produce identical reports. No new tracker merge receipt appeared. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates must certify this combined head."
  "2026-10-22T21:16:33.459Z",codex-agent,"Combined-head CI 39854899743 reached 100% lines/branches/functions across 17 measured files on Node 22 and 26, but failed the existing release-backlog fixture because it assumed changelog:full must directly invoke dist/cli.js. Updated that fixture to execute the actual configured entrypoint and preserve the real tracker same-day suffix/date/link assertions. Removing only the active date-from-version flag from the project entrypoint still makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"self-generation scripts preserve\" test/release-backlog.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1; restored test passes 1/1. Self-review also preserves atomic insert-only collision semantics: a synchronization writer may create the target between read and link; catch EEXIST only at the link operation, recover the original record, clean temporary/lock entries, and propagate other link faults. Reverting only Directory.publish makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"synchronization wins\" test/milestones.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1; restored test passes 1/1. Closed-capture status matching now uses the same case normalization as the generator. Reverting only that status comparison makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"open milestone members\" test/milestones.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1; restored attribution/collision controls pass 2/2. These extend the prior 13 proofs to 16 independent failing reverts. Restored dist rebuilt; build/build:test/docstrings pass. Local npm attempt was stopped unfinished to make these changes, with no failure recorded before stopping; it is not counted as passing."
  "2026-10-22T21:26:51.211Z",codex-agent,"Source 277bee6bdc0fffcd394cfbc6d3b1e5ac60646664 passed CI 39856321732: npm run release:check and bun run release:check on both Node 22 and 26, all four gates 822/822 (3288 executions), zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions across 17 measured files, including the project entrypoint; docstrings cover 20 files/184 declarations. Native Bun CLI/SDK smoke passed 2/2 in each job. Tracker health, audit, pack, changelog/link/date and attestation checks pass. The earlier 821-test matrix stopped only at the old entrypoint assertion; updated actual-entrypoint fixture and active date-flag revert proof now pass in the full matrix. All 16 independent revert proofs and restored controls are recorded above; clock guard proof was additionally rechecked with an independently fingerprinted valid older snapshot. Seven linked command selections have passing receipts, including the corrected suite retries and current edge/date controls. The clean-HOME local npm attempt was stopped unfinished after clean CI passed, with no failure or timeout reported before stopping; not counted as passing. Full PR self-review and real plain-tracker audit integration preserve both milestone and main claim-audit paths. Latest review read has no unresolved thread or outside-diff finding. No manual history repair/re-anchor, thread reply/resolution, PR merge or release. Release claim for orchestrator verification; leave item in_progress."
